@page
@model WoodruffDev.Pages.Services.RetainerModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Retainer-Based Services";
}

<div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="section-label">Service</span>
        <h1>Retainer-Based Services</h1>
        <p>Trusted guidance on call&mdash;because tech challenges don&rsquo;t follow a schedule.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="service-detail fade-in">
            <h2>Service Overview</h2>
            <p>Ongoing architecture support, available when your team needs clarity, feedback, or direction. A retainer gives you a guaranteed block of my time each month, so you always have a seasoned architect to call on when decisions need to be made, reviewed, or challenged.</p>

            <h2>What&rsquo;s Included</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Reserved monthly hours for architecture reviews, team coaching, and decision support</li>
                <li>Priority scheduling and response times</li>
                <li>Ad hoc code and design reviews</li>
                <li>Ongoing strategic guidance as your platform evolves</li>
                <li>Flexible rollover of unused hours (within limits)</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Who This Is For</h2>
            <p>Teams that don&rsquo;t need a full-time architect but do need consistent access to senior technical leadership. Especially useful during growth phases, platform migrations, or post-launch stabilization.</p>

            <div class="service-nav">
                <a href="/Services/ProjectBased">&larr; Project-Based Contracts</a>
                <a href="/Services/Advisory">Advisory &amp; Board Roles &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
